    "q-280220": {
      "dom_id": "step-q280220",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Determine a set of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ that generate a vertical parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and which passes through the point $(-8,8).$ Express your answer in the form $x=2pt,y=p{t}^{2},$ where $p$ is a constant.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}",
      "worked_solution": "The parametric equations of a vertical parabola  that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ are\n\n$$\nx=2pt,\\,y=p{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(-8,8),$ we can substitute $x=-8$ and $y=8$ into the standard parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-8=2pt \\\\ 8=p{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8 & =2pt \\\\ t & =-\\frac{4}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8 & =p{(-\\frac{4}{p})}^{2} \\\\ 8 & =p\\cdot \\frac{16}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ 8 & =\\frac{16}{p} \\\\ p & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=2(2)t,\\,y=(2){t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=4t,\\,y=2{t}^{2}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
