    "q-280226": {
      "dom_id": "step-q280226",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Determine a set of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ that generate the horizontal parabola given by the Cartesian equation ${y}^{2}=32x.$ Express your answer in the form $x=p{t}^{2},y=2pt,$ where $p$ is a constant.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}",
      "worked_solution": "The parametric equations of a horizontal parabola ${y}^{2}=4px$ that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ are\n\n$$\nx=p{t}^{2},\\,y=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nComparing the given Cartesian equation with the general case ${y}^{2}=4px$ and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4px & =32x \\\\ 4p & =32 \\\\ p & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=(8){t}^{2},\\,y=2(8)t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=8{t}^{2},\\,y=16t.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
